{"nodes": [{"id": "service_readme_calculator", "label": "The hosted calculator", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "service/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A stateless HTTP wrapper around agent/tools/ so the Forge app posts dates and status categories and gets figures back rather than a second Monte Carlo in JavaScript. Holds nothing: no credential, no storage, no Jira access. Does no arithmetic."}, {"id": "service_readme_free_text_refused", "label": "Free-text fields are refused, not ignored", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "service/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A 400 naming the field: accepting them quietly would make the service a place customer text lives, which is what the projection exists to prevent. Forge re-attaches summaries by key after the call. Context names (board, sprint, team) are customer strings but not issue text and pass through for display."}, {"id": "service_readme_auth_modes", "label": "SERVICE_AUTH: shared-secret or forge-token", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "service/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "shared-secret cannot tell one customer from another, so it is the local and suite mode; forge-token is the tenant-aware Atlassian invocation token. A verifier returns who the caller is so the access log can name the tenant. Refuses to start without a secret: an open calculator is free compute."}, {"id": "service_readme_forge_token_four_values", "label": "The four FORGE_* values", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "service/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "FORGE_JWKS_URL, FORGE_ISSUER, FORGE_AUDIENCE (the app id ARI, not the bare UUID), FORGE_TENANT_CLAIM (app.installationId, nested, so the verifier walks a dotted path). Environment variables so no unconfirmed value lives in source; the suite mints its own tokens and requires eleven bad shapes to be refused."}, {"id": "service_readme_routes", "label": "Calculator routes", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "service/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "/healthz, /v1/meta, /v1/facts (metrics.facts), /v1/forecast (forecast.build), /v1/forecast-context (selection.forecast_for), /v1/slice (selection.slice_for), /v1/ask (intake.forecast_ask), /v1/sequence (intake.sequence). calendar is on every response because two forecasts under different working weeks are different forecasts."}, {"id": "service_readme_forecast_context_route", "label": "Why /v1/forecast-context exists", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "service/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Choosing the slice is right for serve_live.py (Python, same rules) and wrong for a Node resolver: team_slice plus de-dup by key plus outstanding work from the selected context plus suppressing a window's end date, each a rule that once returned a credible date rather than an error. Moved to selection.py so both reach it; the last logic that should exist twice."}, {"id": "service_readme_limits", "label": "Limits are loud: 413 with a sentence", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "service/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "maxIssues 50,000, maxAsks 12, maxItems 5,000, maxBodyBytes 4 MB; never a truncated calculation since a forecast over half a history looks like one over all of it. The ask cap is intake.MAX_ASKS and the sentence intake.too_many_asks(), so every transport refuses at the same number in the same words."}, {"id": "service_readme_routes_py_travels", "label": "routes.py travels, app.py stays", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "service/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "routes.py is every answer (projection, caps, refusals, answer(path, body)); app.py is the socket, auth verifiers and body limit and adds no key. The Forge function runs routes.py unchanged under WebAssembly, held byte for byte by tests/test_wasm.py, so routes.py may use no sockets, environment or third-party module."}, {"id": "service_readme_region_pinned_deploy", "label": "Cloud Run in two-plus regions, forge-token, scale-to-zero", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "service/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "provision-gcp.sh is the human half; deploy.yml builds, smokes, scans and deploys to every region only if all passed. Fargate retired: no scale-to-zero, 730 hours a month for minutes of work. Forge chooses the region per installation."}, {"id": "service_readme_logging_never_content", "label": "Access log holds counts, never content", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "service/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Method, path, status, issue count, duration. An access log holding issue keys is a copy of the customer's backlog in a log aggregator; tracebacks go to the operator and never into a response because they carry field values."}, {"id": "service_readme_sizing", "label": "Calculator sizing measurements", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "service/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "One team's forecast: 16.2 KB request, 0.25 s, 32 KB response for a 242-issue org; 16.3 KB and 0.74 s for 5,538 issues; intake.sequence four asks 3.07 s, the only call within an order of magnitude of a request timeout."}, {"id": "agent_tools_selection_forecast_for", "label": "selection.forecast_for()", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "service/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "agent_tools_selection_slice_for", "label": "selection.slice_for()", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "service/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "agent_tools_metrics_facts", "label": "metrics.facts()", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "service/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "agent_tools_intake_forecast_ask", "label": "intake.forecast_ask()", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "service/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "service_routes_answer", "label": "routes.answer()", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "service/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "service_app", "label": "service/app.py", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "service/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "service_app_wsgi_app", "label": "app.wsgi_app", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "service/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "tests_test_wasm", "label": "tests/test_wasm.py", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "service/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "service_readme_calculator", "target": "service_readme_free_text_refused", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "service/README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "service_readme_calculator", "target": "service_readme_auth_modes", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "service/README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "service_readme_auth_modes", "target": "service_readme_forge_token_four_values", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "service/README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "service_readme_forge_token_four_values", "target": "service_requirements_pyjwt", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "service/README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "service_readme_forge_token_four_values", "target": "tests_test_service", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "service/README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "service_readme_calculator", "target": "service_readme_routes", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "service/README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "service_readme_routes", "target": "agent_tools_metrics_facts", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "service/README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "service_readme_routes", "target": "agent_tools_forecast_build", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "service/README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "service_readme_routes", "target": "agent_tools_selection_forecast_for", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "service/RE